breaking news right now with new numbers  from the surge of migrants at the  southern border for the month of june  this fox news drone video shows between  400 and 500 migrants per drama  predominantly from venezuela and cuba  crossing into eagle pass texas on  wednesday of course it has become a  familiar sight streams of migrants in  groups of 10 20 30 hundredths from  mexico honduras guatemala and 100 plus  other countries piling into america's  wide open border every day and night  forcing the state of texas to step up  its efforts to defend the state and the  country including governor greg abbott's  executive order which authorizes the  texas national guard and the texas  department of public safety to return  apprehended migrants back to the border  on top of his launching of the 3 billion  border security mission known as  operation lone star the impact of this  wide open border from human trafficking  to death and illicit drug trafficking  has sparked a number of texas counties  to declare this literally an invasion of  america governor greg abbott joins me  right now governor it's good to see you  this morning thank you so much for being  here  my pleasure thank you maria  is this an invasion  listen uh the these counties are dealing  with something that's completely  unprecedented remember this it was just  two years ago we had the the lowest  number of uh people coming across the  border and apprehensions under president  trump uh and then president biden took  over and eliminated all of the policies  that president trump put in place and it  has led uh to this uh unprecedented  overwhelming number of people coming  across the border you gave some of the  numbers uh here's something more  important there's a record number of  people coming across the border from  more than  150 different countries across the  entire globe uh we're seeing over the  fourth of july for example uh  in just the del rio sector which is only  one of five sectors in the state of  texas there were about 5 000 people  either apprehended or or who were got a  ways but it gets worse maria because  look at the number of deaths that we're  dealing with you remember what happened  in the tractor trailer truck or where 53  people lost their lives listen things  like that happen all of the time so much  so that the united nations uh declared  the border between uh texas or the  united states and mexico uh to be the  the worst uh death border and most  dangerous border in the entire world  but on top of things like that we know  about 42 terrorists who have been  apprehended coming across the border  that's not counting the guidaways coming  across the border and then there's the  fentanyl coming across the border and so  yes  we we do have an invasion driven by the  cartels coming across our border that  are pouring people into our country at  unprecedented levels  it's absolutely extraordinary sir and i  know that the word invasion  comes with technical responses from the  government so are you reluctant to say  it's an invasion do you believe this is  an invasion  so the technical reasons for it lie in  the constitution uh there are two parts  of the u.s constitution article four  section 4 article 1 section 10 of the  constitution that use the word invasion  which is the reason why that is used in  that executive order that you said that  i  issued this past week i referenced both  of those plus  i referenced a provision of the texas  constitution that also uses the word  invasion the purpose of of using those  words is it triggers  certain additional ways and strategies  that states  can use their powers to try to protect  against actions such as this that are  driven by the cartels  okay i understand we have put up on the  screen ways that you and your team in  texas are defending the southern border  sir everything uh from obviously your  lone star  plan the operation lone star to  allocating resources deploying thousands  of national guard 